using declaration.description:
ES2027 (Explicit Resource Management — reached Stage 4 in 2026-05, targeted at edition 17+1; already shipping in V8/Node/TypeScript ahead of the formal spec date)
using x = expression;
declares a block-scoped resource that is automatically disposed (its `[Symbol.dispose]()` is called) when control leaves the enclosing block — even via an exception. Similar to a synchronous `try { } finally { resource.dispose(); }`, but composable and can't be forgotten.

await using declaration.description:
ES2027 (Explicit Resource Management — reached Stage 4 in 2026-05, targeted at edition 17+1; already shipping in V8/Node/TypeScript ahead of the formal spec date)
await using x = expression;
like `using`, but disposal calls the resource's `[Symbol.asyncDispose]()` and is awaited. Only valid inside an async function/module, same restriction as top-level `await`.
